WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.820
Well, my mother never did leave during a hurricane.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:09.520
We'd figure we going to ride it out and my sister was going to go stay with Button in Gentilly because we have a duplex in Gentilly.

3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:17.860
We thought we were safe that morning and my mother and I were eating breakfast and all of a sudden we heard, like, this rushing sound.

4
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.340
We were like, "Well, what in the world is this?"

5
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.660
And so when we looked down, the water was just bubbling up through the floor.

6
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.440
And then when we ran to the door, it was like a river.

7
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.560
So I called 911 and they told us to try to get up on the roof.

8
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.400
And I called my sister,

9
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:40.660
and all she could say was that the water had risen real high over there and then the phone went dead and that was it.

10
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.920
That was the only communication we had.

11
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.380
That was that Monday and we didn't get out until that Wednesday morning.

12
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.080
I think either that Wednesday or Thursday morning.

13
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.640
Because I would come and sit on the porch and we thought we were the only ones in the neighborhood.

14
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.180
But in that double . . . that duplex right there, there were people that we saw.

15
00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.220
And we would holler to them across the way.

16
00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.400
They told us to come over but neither one of us could swim and we didn't have a boat.

17
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.740
And so we would sit outside, I would put my mom in her wheelchair and sit her the porch.

18
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:14.880
And a boat passed by, the National Guard, and they picked us up and they brought us right down there by the bridge,

19
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.680
right off of Gentilly Boulevard and dropped us on the bridge on the interstate.

20
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.740
And we had to wait there for a bus, a school bus.

21
00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.400
But they don't tell you where you were going.

22
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:31.780
They put you on a bus and they don't tell you . . . They bring you to a staging area and then somebody comes and whispers to the bus driver in his ear and then he takes off.

23
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.880
And when he's way out, then I asked him, I said, "Well, where are we going?"

24
00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.640
He says "Well, I can tell you now," he said, "We're bringing y'all to the Cajundome in Lafayette."

25
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.540
Which we didn't want to go there.

26
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.100
So I asked him if he could make a pit stop.

27
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:49.520
He crossed the bridge going into Port Allen and Baton Rouge is right across.

28
00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:56.240
So when I knew that we were . . . had crossed over from Baton Rouge to Port Allen, he stopped at this gas station.

29
00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:01.260
I dragged my mother off the bus with her walker because I couldn't bring her wheelchair.

30
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.640
We got to walk to a Days Inn and she said she could make it.

31
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.060
We sat there in the lobby, the lady gave us coffee and stuff because she didn't have any rooms.

32
00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.040
And then hours later she came and told us that she had a room and we were like, "Thank you Jesus!" [laughing]
